[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Always Young]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.34]Why doesn't Aunt Jennifer tell anyone how old she is? | 为什么詹妮弗姑妈不告诉别人她多大岁数？
[00:17.39]My aunt Jennifer is an actress. | 我的姑妈詹妮弗是位演员。
[00:20.95]She must be at least thirty-five years old. | 她至少也有35岁了。
[00:25.21]In spite of this, she often appears on the stage as a young girl. | 尽管如此，她却常在舞台上扮演小姑娘。
[00:31.68]Jennifer will have to take part in a new play soon. | 詹妮弗很快又要参加一部新戏的演出了。
[00:36.10]This time, she will be a girl of seventeen. | 这一次，她将扮演一个17岁的少女。
[00:41.18]In the play, she must appear in a bright red dress and long black stockings. | 演出时她必须穿着大红色的裙子和黑色的长筒袜。
[00:49.17]Last year in another play, | 去年在另一出戏里，
[00:51.70]she had to wear short socks and a bright, orange-coloured dress. | 她不得不穿短袜和一条色彩鲜艳的橘红色连衣裙。
[00:58.45]If anyone ever asks her how old she is, | 一旦有人问起她的年龄，
[01:02.55]she always answers, 'Darling, it must be terrible to be grown up!' | 她总是回答：“亲爱的，长大成人太可怕了！”
